  "nl_text": "This schema is for a database that stores information about an enterprise, its employees, their roles, and their attendance records. The database is called \"rschema_0493\" and has five tables: enterprise, role, employee, attendance_record, and to-do_item.\nThe enterprise table contains information about the enterprise, including its creation time, ID, and name. The role table contains information about the roles of the employees, including their daily working hours, hourly wage, lunch time, and ID. The employee table contains information about the employees, including their creation time, email, ID, identification number, name, password, role ID, update time, and foreign keys to the enterprise and role tables.\nThe attendance_record table contains information about the attendance records of the employees, including their check-in location, check-in time, employee ID, remarks, and primary key (employee ID and check-in time). The to-do_item table contains information about the to-do items of the employees, including their completion status, creation time, employee ID, task description, update time, and primary key (employee ID and creation time).\nThe foreign keys in the employee and attendance_record tables reference the enterprise and role tables, respectively, while the foreign keys in the to-do_item table reference the employee table. The foreign key constraints are set to cascade on update and restrict on delete, ensuring that the data in the child tables is consistent with the data in the parent tables.\nOverall, this schema provides a comprehensive structure for storing and managing information about an enterprise, its employees, and their attendance records, as well as their to-do items.",
  "gold_question": "The business management system is described as follows:\nThe system manages multiple enterprises, with enterprise information including name and creation time.\nEach enterprise has multiple employees, with employee information including name, email, password, identification number, role, creation time, and update time.\nEach role has different hourly wages, daily working hours, and lunchtime.\nEach employee has multiple attendance records, with attendance record information including check-in time, remarks, and check-in location.\nAdditionally, employees can create to-do items, with to-do item information including task description, completion status, creation time, and update time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0493.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0493\nCREATE TABLE `enterprise` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `daily_working_hours` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `hourly_wage` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `lunch_time` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `identification_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `enterprise_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`enterprise_id`) REFERENCES `enterprise` (`id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attendance_record` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `check_in_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `check_in_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `check_in_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `to_do_item` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `task_description` text NOT NULL,\n  `completion_status` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `creation_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `to_do_item_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
